  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "l01",
      "start": 0.2,
      "end": 3.825,
      "text": "Leave the fridge open on a hot day, and the kitchen gets warmer.",
      "words": 13,
      "words_per_s": 3.59,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.5
    },
    {
      "id": "l02",
      "start": 4.1,
      "end": 5.926,
      "text": "So how can a cold box heat a room?",
      "words": 9,
      "words_per_s": 4.93,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 19.4
    },
    {
      "id": "l03",
      "start": 6.3,
      "end": 8.756,
      "text": "A fridge doesn't make cold. It pumps heat.",
      "words": 8,
      "words_per_s": 3.26,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.6
    },
    {
      "id": "l04",
      "start": 9.15,
      "end": 13.41,
      "text": "Cold fluid in the inside coils evaporates, soaking up your food's heat.",
      "words": 12,
      "words_per_s": 2.82,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.0
    },
    {
      "id": "l05",
      "start": 13.8,
      "end": 18.765,
      "text": "A compressor squeezes it hotter than the room, and coils outside the box release that heat.",
      "words": 16,
      "words_per_s": 3.22,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.1
    },
    {
      "id": "l06",
      "start": 19.15,
      "end": 22.629,
      "text": "Door open, that heat just circles back, plus the motor's own.",
      "words": 11,
      "words_per_s": 3.16,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.4
    },
    {
      "id": "l07",
      "start": 23.0,
      "end": 25.735,
      "text": "That's why air conditioners dump their heat outdoors.",
      "words": 8,
      "words_per_s": 2.93,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.7
    },
    {
      "id": "l08",
      "start": 26.45,
      "end": 29.733,
      "text": "Download Recall to turn your study material into lessons.",
      "words": 9,
      "words_per_s": 2.74,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.6
    }
  ],
